<title>BELGIUM: Belgian SGB sells 1.4% of Suez.</title>
<headline>Belgian SGB sells 1.4% of Suez.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian holding company Societe Generale de Belgique SA said on Wednesday it had sold 2,182,386 shares, or 1.4 percent, of its French parent Cie. de Suez to another Suez subsidiary.</p>
<p>&quot;This transaction was carried out at market price and will have a positive influence on SGB's accounts,&quot; SGB said in a statement.</p>
<p>SGB is 62.6 percent held by Suez. SGB said earlier this year it planned to sell its Suez stake.</p>
<p>-- Nick Antonovics, Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6817, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
